### 2. Real-Time Messaging (Firebase)
Firebase handles the "real-time" aspect automatically via WebSockets.

**Setup:** Initialize Firebase in your app.
```javascript
import { getDatabase, ref, push, onValue } from "firebase/database";

const db = getDatabase();

// Sending a message
function sendMessage(chatId, userId, text) {
  push(ref(db, 'messages/' + chatId), {
    userId,
    text,
    timestamp: Date.now()
  });
}

// Listening for messages (Real-time)
useEffect(() => {
  const messagesRef = ref(db, 'messages/' + chatId);
  onValue(messagesRef, (snapshot) => {
    const data = snapshot.val();
    setMessages(Object.values(data));
  });
}, []);
```

