Mutexes trigger kernel-level context switches. Use `std::atomic` with memory barriers (`memory_order_acquire`/`release`) to ensure thread safety without blocking.

#### 2. Cache Line Padding
Modern CPUs fetch data in 64-byte chunks. If your `head` and `tail` pointers sit on the same cache line, you get **"False Sharing,"** which destroys performance.
