The code above uses `rte_mbuf`. DPDK manages a pool of pre-allocated memory buffers. When a packet arrives, the NIC DMA engine writes the packet directly into one of these buffers. Your application processes the pointer to that buffer, meaning **the packet data is never copied in memory**.

#### 2. CPU Pinning (Affinity)
Standard OS schedulers will move your process between CPU cores, causing cache misses. You must pin your forwarding thread to a specific physical core:
```c
