If you need to handle TCP/UDP, do **not** use the Linux kernel stack. Use a user-space TCP/IP stack like **[f-stack](https://github.com/f-stack/f-stack)** or **[mtcp](https://github.com/eunyoung14/mtcp)**, which are designed to run on top of DPDK.

