#### C. Data Filtering (Moving Average)
Raw sensor data is often noisy. Instead of using the raw value immediately, implement a simple moving average:
```c
float get_filtered_value(float new_sample) {
    static float buffer[5] = {0};
    static int index = 0;
    static float sum = 0;

    sum -= buffer[index];
    buffer[index] = new_sample;
    sum += buffer[index];
    index = (index + 1) % 5;

    return sum / 5.0f;
}
```

#### D. Error Handling
Always check if your sensor is actually responding. If `HAL_Sensor_Read()` returns an error code or a NaN (Not a Number), your firmware should handle it gracefully rather than crashing.

