### 2. The Physics World (The Plugin Core)
This class manages the integration (updating positions based on forces). We use **Semi-Implicit Euler integration**, which is more stable than standard Euler for games.

```cpp
class PhysicsPlugin {
public:
    void Update(std::vector<PhysicsBody*>& bodies, float deltaTime) {
        const glm::vec3 gravity(0.0f, -9.81f, 0.0f);

        for (auto* body : bodies) {
            if (body->isStatic) continue;

            // 1. Apply Gravity
            body->ApplyForce(gravity * body->mass);

            // 2. Calculate Acceleration (F = ma -> a = F/m)
            glm::vec3 acceleration = body->force * body->inverseMass;

            // 3. Update Velocity
            body->velocity += acceleration * deltaTime;

            // 4. Update Position (This would link to your Transform component)
            // transform.position += body->velocity * deltaTime;

            // 5. Reset Force for next frame
            body->force = glm::vec3(0.0f);
        }
    }
};
```

