### 3. The Payment Service (Core Logic)
The key here is the **Idempotency Key**. If a client retries a request due to a network timeout, the system must return the existing result rather than creating a duplicate charge.

```java
@Service
public class PaymentService {

    @Autowired
    private PaymentRepository repository;

    @Transactional
    public PaymentResponse processPayment(PaymentRequest request, String idempotencyKey) {
        // 1. Check if request already processed
        Optional<Payment> existing = repository.findById(UUID.fromString(idempotencyKey));
        if (existing.isPresent()) {
            return mapToResponse(existing.get());
        }

        // 2. Create record in PENDING state
        Payment payment = new Payment(request, idempotencyKey, PaymentStatus.PENDING);
        repository.save(payment);

        // 3. Publish to Message Broker (e.g., Kafka) for async processing
        // This decouples the API response from the slow banking network
        eventPublisher.send("payment-processing-topic", payment);

        return new PaymentResponse(payment.getPaymentId(), "ACCEPTED");
    }
}
```

